 Or if your book came at the DVD, be sure to look at that.

581
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:00,720
 Now we're going to be looking

582
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:02,960
 at the posterior compartment muscles.

583
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:06,640
 The consists of four superficial and four deep muscles.

584
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:08,360
 They're all innervated by the radial nerve

585
00:23:08,360 --> 00:23:11,400
 or its branches and more than half of the posterior compartment

586
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:14,760
 muscles, they arise from a common extensor origin tendon

587
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:16,600
 that's attached to the posterior surface

588
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:18,720
 of the lateral epicondyl of the humerus

589
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:20,320
 and the adjacent fascia.

590
00:23:20,320 --> 00:23:21,920
 The extensor tendons are held in place

591
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,560
 at the posterior aspect of the wrist

592
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:25,120
 by the extensor retinaculum,

593
00:23:25,120 --> 00:23:26,880
 which prevents the bolstering of the attendants

594
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:28,840
 when the wrist is hyper-extended.

595
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,320
 The extensor muscles of the fingers

596
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:32,640
 end in a broad hood over the dorsal side of the digits

597
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:35,040
 called the extensor expansion.

598
