00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:11,960
 that may have come with your book,

611
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:14,440
 or you can always look for it on YouTube.

612
00:24:14,440 --> 00:24:16,320
 So the first superficial muscle that we're

613
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:19,600
 going to be looking at is the extensor carb by Radialis Longus.

614
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,680
 And this parallels with the brachior Radialis

615
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:24,800
 on the lateral forearm, and it may blend with it.

616
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:28,480
 Its origin is a lateral supercondular ridge of the humerus,

617
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:31,720
 and its insertion is the base of the second metacarpal.

618
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:35,280
 Now its prime actions are to extend and abduct the wrist.

619
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:36,800
 It extends the wrist in conjunction

620
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:39,440
 with the extensor carb by Oneris, and it

621
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:43,640
 abducts the wrist in conjunction with the flexor carb by Radialis.

622
00:24:43,640 --> 00:24:46,040
 And it's innervated by the Radial nerve.

623
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:48,280
 The extensor carb by Radialis Brevis muscle

624
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:51,480
 lies deep to the extensor carb by Radialis Longus,

625
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:53,360
 and is somewhat shorter than it.

626
00:24:53,360 --> 00:24:55,760
 Its origin is a lateral epicano of the humerus,

627
00:24:55,760 --> 00:24:58,760
 and its insertion is the base of the third metacarpal.

628
00:24:58,760 --> 00:25:01,680
 It's innervated by the deep branch of the Radial nerve,

629
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:05,400
 and its prime action is to extend and abduct the wrist.

630
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:08,840
 It also acts as a synergist with the extensor carb by Radialis

631
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:11,560
 Longus to steady the wrist during finger flexion.

632
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:14,960
 The extensor digitorum lies medial to the extensor carb by Radialis

633
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:16,040
 Brevis.

634
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:19,280
 A detached portion of it, called the extensor digiti

635
00:25:19,280 --> 00:25:22,240
 minimae, it extends to the little finger, as you can see,

636
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:23,560
 going right down here.

637
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:26,120
 Its origin is a lateral epicondale of the humerus,

638
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:27,960
 and its insertion is by four tendons

639
00:25:27,960 --> 00:25:30,880
 into the extensor expansion and the distal phalanges

640
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:33,680
 of fingers two, three, four, and five.

641
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:37,000
 Its action is that it's a prime mover of the finger extension,

642
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:40,680
 and it also extends the wrist and can abduct the fingers,

643
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:43,080
 so it's when you're flaring your fingers.

644
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:46,120
 And it's innervated by the posterior intra osteos nerve.

645
00:25:46,120 --> 00:25:49,400
 This long slender muscle is extensor carb by onaris.

646
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:52,080
 It's the most medial of the superficial posterior muscles.

647
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:54,320
 Its origin is a lateral epicondale of the humerus,

648
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:56,520
 and the posterior border of the ona.

649
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:59,560
 Its insertion is the base of the fifth metacarpal.

650
00:25:59,560 --> 00:26:01,760
 Its action is to extend the wrist in conjunction

651
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,640
 with the extensor carb by Radialis,

652
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:05,480
 and it adducts the wrist in conjunction

653
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:07,520
 with the flexor carb by onaris.

654
00:26:07,520 --> 00:26:11,800
 And it's innervated by the posterior intra osteos nerve.

655
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:14,720
 And there's more animations for you guys to look at,

656
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:16,160
 so please be sure to look at this.

