00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:45,240
 So the first one we're gonna look at is the supinator.

668
00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:47,880
 And this is a deep muscle at the posterior aspect

669
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:49,960
 of the elbow, and it's largely concealed

670
00:26:49,960 --> 00:26:51,880
 by the superficial muscles.

671
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:54,800
 Its origin is the lateral epicondyle of the humerus

672
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:56,720
 and the proximal ulna.

673
00:26:56,720 --> 00:27:00,040
 Its insertion is gonna be the proximal end of the radius.

674
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:02,880
 And its main action assist is the biceps brachia

675
00:27:02,880 --> 00:27:05,040
 to forcibly supinate the forearm.

676
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:07,720
 It works alone in slow supination also,

677
00:27:07,720 --> 00:27:10,720
 and it's an antagonist of the pronator muscles.

678
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:13,760
 It's innervated by the posterior interosseous nerve.

679
00:27:13,760 --> 00:27:16,360
 Next, we have the abductor policies longest,

680
00:27:16,360 --> 00:27:18,080
 and this is lateral and parallel

681
00:27:18,080 --> 00:27:19,920
 to the extensor policies longest,

682
00:27:19,920 --> 00:27:22,760
 and it's just distal to the supinator.

683
00:27:22,760 --> 00:27:26,080
 Its origin is a posterior surface of the radius and ulna

684
00:27:26,080 --> 00:27:28,160
 and the interosseous membrane.

685
00:27:28,160 --> 00:27:30,800
 Its insertion is the base of the first metacarpal

686
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:32,440
 and the trapezium.

687
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:35,040
 And its action is to abduct and extend the thumb,

688
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:38,120
 and it's innervated by the posterior interosseous nerve.

689
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:41,520
 The extensor policies brevis and the extensor policies longest

690
00:27:41,520 --> 00:27:44,640
 is overlain by the extensor carpi ulneris.

691
00:27:44,640 --> 00:27:47,240
 Its origin is the dorsal shaft of the radius and ulna

692
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:49,000
 and the interosseous membrane.

693
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,840
 Its insertion is the base of the proximal

694
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:52,640
 and distal feelings of the thumb.

695
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:54,280
 Its prime action is to extend the thumb

696
00:27:54,280 --> 00:27:57,200
 and it's innervated by the posterior interosseous nerve.

697
00:27:57,200 --> 00:28:00,040
 Finally, we have the extensor indices right over here.

698
00:28:00,040 --> 00:28:02,960
 And this is a tiny muscle that's rising close to the wrist.

699
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:05,880
 Its origin is the posterior surface of the distal ulna

700
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:07,840
 and the interosseous membrane.

701
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:11,000
 Its insertion is the extensor expansion of the index finger

702
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:13,680
 and it joins the tendon of the extensor digitorum.

703
00:28:13,680 --> 00:28:16,200
 Its prime action is to extend the index finger

704
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:18,720
 and it assists in wrist extension.

705
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:23,000
 And it's innervated by the posterior interosseous nerve.

