752
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:34,560
 Now we're going to be looking at the intrinsic muscles

753
00:30:34,560 --> 00:30:37,320
 with the hand, which are responsible for the fine moments

754
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:38,520
 of the fingers.

755
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:41,200
 All these small muscles are entirely in the palm

756
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:43,160
 and none on the hands, dorsal side.

757
00:30:43,160 --> 00:30:46,200
 These small weak muscles mostly control precise movements,

758
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:48,000
 leaving the powerful movements of the fingers

759
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:49,480
 to the forearm muscles.

760
00:30:49,480 --> 00:30:52,160
 The intrinsic muscles include the main abductors

761
00:30:52,160 --> 00:30:54,800
 and adductors of the fingers, as well as muscles

762
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:57,000
 that produce the movement of opposition, which

763
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:59,360
 is moving the thumb towards the little finger.

764
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:01,240
 In addition to that, it allows for movements

765
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:03,160
 that enables your grip objects in the palm,

766
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:06,320
 so as in when you're holding a baseball bat.

767
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:07,800
 Some movements are defined differently

768
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:09,160
 from the movements of the other fingers,

769
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:12,080
 because the thumb lies at a right angle to the rest of the hand.

770
00:31:12,080 --> 00:31:14,680
 The thumb flexes by bending medally along the palm,

771
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:17,800
 not by bending anteriorly as the other fingers do.

772
00:31:17,800 --> 00:31:20,480
 And the thumb extends by pointing laterally,

773
00:31:20,480 --> 00:31:23,800
 not posteriorly, as the other fingers do.

774
00:31:23,800 --> 00:31:25,200
 The interesting muscles of the palm

775
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:27,160
 are divided into three groups.

776
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:29,920
 Those in the thinare eminence, which is the ball of the thumb,

777
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:31,760
 those that are in the hyper-thinare eminence,

778
00:31:31,760 --> 00:31:33,400
 which is the ball of the little fingers,

779
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:35,520
 and those that are in the mid palm.

780
00:31:35,520 --> 00:31:37,120
 The thinner and the hyper-thinare muscles

781
00:31:37,120 --> 00:31:39,400
 are almost mirror images of one another.

782
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:42,040
 Each contain a small flexor, an abductor,

783
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:43,800
 and an opponent's muscle.

784
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:46,240
 The mid-palmer muscles, called the lumberkels

785
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:48,520
 and the introsia, they extend our fingers

786
00:31:48,520 --> 00:31:50,680
 at the interphalangeal joints.

787
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:53,000
 The introsia are also the main finger

788
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:56,120
 abductors and adductors.

789
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:58,120
 We're going to start off by looking at the thinare muscles

790
00:31:58,120 --> 00:31:59,080
 in the ball of the thumb.

791
00:31:59,080 --> 00:32:00,840
 And the first muscle that we're going to be looking at

792
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:05,080
 is the adductor pauses, brothers, which is right over here.

793
00:32:05,080 --> 00:32:07,640
 And this is a lateral muscle of the thinare group.

794
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:08,680
 It's superficial.

795
00:32:08,680 --> 00:32:10,880
 So when you're abducting your thumb,

796
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:13,760
 so when you bring your thumb towards your index finger,

797
00:32:13,760 --> 00:32:16,200
 that muscle that you see that's bulging out the muscles.

798
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:17,200
 This is that muscle.

799
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:19,640
 This is the adductor pauses, brothers.

800
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:21,920
 Its origin is a flexor retinaculum

801
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:23,480
 and the nearby carples.

802
00:32:23,480 --> 00:32:25,520
 And its insertion is the lateral base

803
00:32:25,520 --> 00:32:27,880
 of the thumb's proximal phalanx.

804
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:29,800
 Its main action is to abduct the thumbs

805
00:32:29,800 --> 00:32:31,680
 at the carpal metacarpal joint.

806
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:33,760
 And it's innervated by the median nerve.

807
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:36,240
 Next, we have the flexor pauses brevis.

808
00:32:36,240 --> 00:32:39,440
 And this is the medial and deep muscle of the thinare group.

809
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:42,920
 Its origin is a flexor retinaculum and nearby carples.

810
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:44,920
 And the insertion is the lateral side

811
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:47,840
 of the base of the proximal phalanx of the thumb.

812
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:50,000
 Its prime action is that it flexes the thumb

813
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:54,000
 at the carpal metacarpal and the metacarpal phalanxial joints.

814
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:55,520
 And it's innervated by the median

815
00:32:55,520 --> 00:32:57,440
 and in occasionally the ulnar nerve.

816
00:32:57,440 --> 00:32:59,280
 Next, we have the adductor pauses.

817
00:32:59,280 --> 00:33:02,440
 This is a fan-shaped muscle with horizontal fibers.

818
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:04,640
 Its distal to the other thinare muscles.

819
00:33:04,640 --> 00:33:07,200
 And it has oblique and transverse heads.

820
00:33:07,200 --> 00:33:10,160
 Its origin is a capitate bone and the bones of metacarpals

821
00:33:10,160 --> 00:33:14,320
 2, 3, and 4, in addition to the front of metacarpal 3.

822
00:33:14,320 --> 00:33:16,040
 And its insertion is the medial side

823
00:33:16,040 --> 00:33:18,400
 of the base of the proximal phalanx of the thumb.

824
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:22,280
 As for its action, it adducts and helps to pose the thumb.

825
00:33:22,280 --> 00:33:24,480
 And it's innervated by the ulnar nerve.

826
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:27,520
 The opponent's policies is deeply the adductor pauses

827
00:33:27,520 --> 00:33:29,600
 brevis on metacarpal 1.

828
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:32,800
 Its origin is a flexor retinaculum and the trapezium.

829
00:33:32,800 --> 00:33:34,800
 And its insertion is the whole anterior side

830
00:33:34,800 --> 00:33:35,800
 of metacarpal 1.

831
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:37,540
 Its prime movement is opposition.

832
00:33:37,540 --> 00:33:39,560
 So this is the muscle that allows you to move your thumb

833
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:41,480
 and touch the tip of your little finger.

834
00:33:41,480 --> 00:33:43,840
 It's innervated by the median or occasionally

835
00:33:43,840 --> 00:33:44,840
 the ulnar nerve.

836
00:33:44,840 --> 00:33:47,080
 Now we're going to be looking at the hypoethenar muscles

837
00:33:47,080 --> 00:33:48,600
 in the ball of the little finger.

838
00:33:48,600 --> 00:33:50,160
 And the first one that we're going to be looking at

839
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:53,080
 is the abductor digitai minimae.

840
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:55,560
 And this is the medial muscle of the hypoethenar group.

841
00:33:55,560 --> 00:33:57,000
 And it's superficial.

842
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:58,920
 Its origin is a pissiform bone.

843
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:00,680
 And its insertion is the medial side

844
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:03,240
 of the proximal phalanx of the little finger.

845
00:34:03,240 --> 00:34:06,400
 And its main action is to abduct the little fingers

846
00:34:06,400 --> 00:34:08,560
 at the metacarpal phalanxial joint.

847
00:34:08,560 --> 00:34:10,720
 And it's innervated by the ulnar nerve.

848
00:34:10,720 --> 00:34:12,720
 The flexor digitai minimum brevis.

849
00:34:12,720 --> 00:34:15,480
 It's a lateral deep muscle of the hypoethenar group.

850
00:34:15,480 --> 00:34:18,720
 Its origin is the hyamate bone and the flexor retinaculum.

851
00:34:18,720 --> 00:34:22,080
 Its insertion is same as the abductor digitai minimae.

852
00:34:22,080 --> 00:34:24,160
 And its action is to flex the little fingers

853
00:34:24,160 --> 00:34:26,200
 at the metacarpal phalanxial joint.

854
00:34:26,200 --> 00:34:28,680
 And it's also innervated by the ulnar nerve.

855
00:34:28,680 --> 00:34:30,480
 The opponent's digitai minimae is

856
00:34:30,480 --> 00:34:32,920
 deep through the abductor digitai minimae.

857
00:34:32,920 --> 00:34:36,440
 Its origin is the same as the flexor digitai minimae brevis.

858
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:38,920
 And its insertion is most of the length of the medial side

859
00:34:38,920 --> 00:34:40,680
 of the metacarpal five.

860
00:34:40,680 --> 00:34:43,080
 Its action is that it helps in opposition.

861
00:34:43,080 --> 00:34:46,720
 It brings metacarpal five towards the thumb to cup the hand.

862
00:34:46,720 --> 00:34:49,000
 And it's also innervated by the ulnar nerve.

863
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:51,360
 Now we're going to be moving on to the mid-palmer muscles.

864
00:34:51,360 --> 00:34:53,080
 And the first muscle we're going to be looking at

865
00:34:53,080 --> 00:34:54,600
 is the lumbercalls.

866
00:34:54,600 --> 00:34:57,240
 We have four of these warm-shaped muscles in our palm,

867
00:34:57,240 --> 00:34:59,880
 one to each finger with the exception of the thumb,

868
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:02,040
 usually because they originate from the tendons

869
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:03,080
 of another muscle.

870
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:05,280
 So here you can see the first lumbercalls.

871
00:35:05,280 --> 00:35:07,080
 This is the second lumbercalls.

872
00:35:07,080 --> 00:35:08,800
 And this is the third lumbercall.

873
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:11,240
 And this is the fourth lumbercall.

874
00:35:11,240 --> 00:35:14,960
 And as you can see, the origin is a lateral side

875
00:35:14,960 --> 00:35:16,960
 of each tendon of the flexor digitorum

876
00:35:16,960 --> 00:35:18,200
 profoundest in the palm.

877
00:35:18,200 --> 00:35:21,160
 Its insertion is a lateral edge of the extensor expansion

878
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:24,800
 on the proximal failings of fingers two, three, four, and five.

879
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:26,720
 And its action is to flex the fingers

880
00:35:26,720 --> 00:35:28,840
 at the metacarpal phalangeal joints.

881
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:32,720
 But it also extends the fingers at the intra-phalangeal joints.

882
00:35:32,720 --> 00:35:35,240
 It's innervated by the lateral two million nerves

883
00:35:35,240 --> 00:35:37,640
 and the median two ulnar nerves.

884
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:41,760
 The palma or interossii are four long, quench-shaped muscles

885
00:35:41,760 --> 00:35:43,780
 in the spaces between the metacarpals.

886
00:35:43,780 --> 00:35:46,320
 They lie ventral to the dorsal interossii.

887
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:48,280
 Its origins on the side of each metacarpal

888
00:35:48,280 --> 00:35:50,120
 that faces the metac axis of the hand.

889
00:35:50,120 --> 00:35:52,160
 But it's absent from metacarpal three.

890
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:54,040
 Its insertion is the extensor expansion

891
00:35:54,040 --> 00:35:57,120
 on the first failings of each finger, except for finger three,

892
00:35:57,120 --> 00:35:59,600
 and on the side facing the metac axis of the hand.

893
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:02,480
 As for the action, these are the adductors of the fingers.

894
00:36:02,480 --> 00:36:05,000
 It pulls the fingers in towards the third digit.

895
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,680
 It also acts with the lumbercalls

896
00:36:06,680 --> 00:36:09,240
 to extend the fingers at the intra-phalangeal joints

897
00:36:09,240 --> 00:36:11,760
 and flexes them at the metacarpal phalangeal joints.

898
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:14,840
 For its nerves of flight, it's innervated by the ulnar nerve.

899
00:36:14,840 --> 00:36:17,160
 The dorsal interossii are four bipenic muscles

900
00:36:17,160 --> 00:36:19,440
 that are filling the spaces between the metacarpals.

901
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:21,120
 These are the deepest palm muscles.

902
00:36:21,120 --> 00:36:23,320
 They're also visible on the dorsal side of the hand.

903
00:36:23,320 --> 00:36:25,800
 Its origin is the size of the metacarpals,

904
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:28,240
 and the insertion are the extensor expansion

905
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:31,520
 over the proximal failings of fingers two, three, and four

906
00:36:31,520 --> 00:36:34,120
 on the sides opposite the metac axis of the hand.

907
00:36:34,120 --> 00:36:36,160
 But on both sides of finger three.

908
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:37,320
 And you can see that over here.

909
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:39,240
 So here's the proximal failings.

910
00:36:39,240 --> 00:36:41,280
 And it's on the opposite side of the mid-axis.

911
00:36:41,280 --> 00:36:42,320
 This is the mid-axis.

912
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:44,760
 So this is the opposite side of the mid-axis.

913
00:36:44,760 --> 00:36:47,200
 With the exception of-- so you can see it over here.

914
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:48,880
 This is the opposite of the mid-axis,

915
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:50,680
 the opposite of the mid-axis.

916
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:52,240
 With the exception of the third digit,

917
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:53,280
 we use your middle finger.

918
00:36:53,280 --> 00:36:54,680
 It's on both sides.

919
00:36:54,680 --> 00:36:57,000
 And its prime action is to abduct the fingers

920
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:58,720
 or diverge the fingers.

921
00:36:58,720 --> 00:37:01,040
 In addition to that, it also extends the fingers

922
00:37:01,040 --> 00:37:02,760
 at the intra-phalangeal joints.

923
00:37:02,760 --> 00:37:05,640
 And it flexes them at the metacarpal phalangeal joints.

924
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:08,520
 For a nervous apply, it's innervated by the ulnar nerve.

925
